       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum recommended dose of 200 mg. It could seriously harm the patient, and the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmias. A confirmation from someone who isn't the prescribing clinician doesn't make that dose safe.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **If a prescriber wants this dose**, they can enter the order themselves. A pharmacist will also need to review it. I can't enter it on their behalf without that clinical oversight.\n- **If you meant a different dose**, tell me and I'll enter it. A typical dose is 50\u2013200 mg once daily.\n- **If you have a concern about the patient's treatment**, I can help you reach the treating team or the pharmacy."
      }
     ],
